within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.G_GenitoUrinarySystemAndSexHormones.G04B_Urologicals.G04BE07_Apomorphine;
model Apomorphine_Nasser2024_PD_updrs_part_iii
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Nasser_2024 :: UPDRS Part III (UPDRS motor scores)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 24.3,      // [1]
    Emax = -1,  // [1]
    EC50 = 1.07e-05,  // [kg/m3; ng/mL × 1e-06]
    gamma = 3,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng/mL per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 110, Interval = 0.22),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Apomorphine_Nasser2024_PD_updrs_part_iii</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Nasser A et al., <i>Journal of pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics 51(4):385–393</i> 2024 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10928-024-09914-x\">doi:10.1007/s10928-024-09914-x</a>) — UPDRS motor scores against apomorphine ng/mL — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       24.3          drug-free response (baseline) (B0, Q324)
  Emax  =          1          maximal effect term (Emax, Q323)
  EC50  =       10.7 ng/mL    exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC50, Q321)
  gamma =          3          Hill coefficient (g, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng/mL of apomorphine per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 24.3   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (10.7 ng/mL)  response 23.8
  exposure -> infinity  response 23.3</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Nasser_2024: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Apomorphine_Nasser2024_PD_updrs_part_iii;
